course: dictionary
lesson: 2266
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can wear different coats. Creation means the act of making something new, a thing someone has made, or, in religion, the making of the world by God. The words around it tell you which meaning is meant. «Her creation was a painting of a sunset» means a thing she made.
explain: «The creation of the new bridge took three years» is about the act of making it. «Some Christians hope God will make all creation new» means the whole world and everything in it. Check by asking: what is being made, and who is making it?
explain: Creation with a capital C, as in «the Creation», is a religious word. In RE the creation story tells of six days of making and one day of rest. Many believers say science and faith answer different questions, so both can be talked about in school.
fact: Creation means the act of making something new.
fact: A creation is a thing someone has made, like a painting, a cake or a story.
fact: «The Creation», with a capital C, means the making of the world by God, told in Genesis.
fact: «All creation» can mean the whole world and everything in it.
fact: Christians say the earth is God's creation, and people are its stewards: they look after it, as you would look after something that belongs to someone else.
exercise: «Her creation was a painting of a sunset.» What is a creation here? | The end of a story | A kind of cloud | The making of the world by God | *A thing someone has made
exercise: «The creation of the new bridge took three years.» What does creation mean here? | The whole world and everything in it | A holiday | *The act of making something new | A painting in a gallery
exercise: «People are made last, so many Christians see them as the high point of creation.» What does creation mean here? | A thing someone has painted | The making of the world by God | *The whole world and everything in it | The act of drawing
test: «Some Christians hope God will make all creation new.» What does all creation mean? | A small garden | A school trip | A cake recipe | *The whole world and everything in it
test: In RE, the creation story tells how the world was made. How long was the making, in the story? | *Six days of making and one day of rest | A year of rest | Ten days of painting | Three days of making
exam: In art class the teacher says, «Your creation is lovely.» What does creation mean here? | A type of weather | *A thing you have made | Staying still and quiet | The whole world and everything in it
